    "explanation": "the 91.1% figure is carried almost entirely by ONE_SIDED observations, where the leader is right ~94.6% of the time and has NO ASK in 100% of cases -- so the accurate leader cannot be bought at any price, and the single executable side is the loser in 94.6% of them at an average 0.186. The executable-favorite subset is the TWO_SIDED minority, where both outcomes are buyable across a ~0.35 spread and the leader is close to a coin flip. The book goes two-sided precisely when the outcome is undecided: within TWO_SIDED, winners sit a median $7.59 from the strike on the proxy and losers $1.58.",
